generatedCommentsNodes.comment:
The `createDummyRollupIndex()` helper is called from three different test methods within the same test class. Each call issues `PUT /dummy-rollup-index`, which will throw a `ResponseException` (400 `resource_already_exists_exception`) if the index already exists from a prior test in the same cluster. Depending on the test framework's per-test cleanup behavior, the second and third invocations may fail. Consider making the creation idempotent, e.g. by catching the "already exists" response or checking for index existence first:
```java
private static void createDummyRollupIndex() throws IOException {
    Request req = new Request("PUT", "dummy-rollup-index");
    req.setJsonEntity(...);
    try {
        client().performRequest(req);
    } catch (ResponseException e) {
        if (e.getResponse().getStatusLine().getStatusCode() != 400) {
            throw e;
        }
        // index already exists, safe to ignore
    }
}
```

